-- allium: 3
-- access.allium — who may see and do what: access modes, the derived permission of a party on a repository per unit, owner visibility, and the authorization gates every other module relies on.
--
-- Scope: the authorisation model of the forge.
--   * AccessMode (none < read < write < admin < owner) and how a party's
--     effective mode on a repository is derived, per unit.
--   * Grant sources: site administrator, repository owner (user), the owning
--     organization's owner team and admin teams, team access modes and per-unit
--     team access (incl. teams that include all repositories), collaborators,
--     the public default for signed-in users, the "everyone may write" unit
--     setting (globally writable wiki), anonymous read of public repositories.
--   * Denials and reductions: private repositories, owner visibility
--     (limited/private users and organizations), restricted users,
--     REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW, disabled units, archived repositories (read-only),
--     mirrors (code is read-only), blocked users, credential restrictions
--     (fine-grained tokens / authorized integrations: public-only and
--     listed-repository reach), Actions task tokens.
--   * Organization, team, profile and site-administration gates
--     (reqOrgOwnership, reqOrgMembership, reqTeamMembership, reqSiteAdmin,
--     reqSelfOrAdmin, individual-owner visibility).
--   * The materialised explicit-access index (Forgejo's `access` table) and
--     exactly when it is recalculated.
--   * The operation -> required-permission table (see "Authorization table").
--
-- Includes: AccessMode, OperationClass, GrantBasis, CredentialRestriction,
--   RepoAccess, AccessDecision, AnonymousVisitor, ForgeComponent,
--   AuthorizationPolicy contract.
--
-- Excludes:
--   - Token scope categories/levels and how a token is parsed (owned by
--     authentication; referenced here through `CredentialRestriction` and the
--     scope column of the authorization table).
--   - Branch protection / push rules / maintainer-edit delegation details
--     (owned by code and pulls; referenced as the branch-level write gate).
--   - Package-registry permission resolution (owned by packages; it reuses
--     `can_see_owner` and org unit permission defined here).
--   - The `ignore team` variant of team-access recalculation: an artefact of
--     recalculating before the team link is deleted; a rebuild recalculates
--     after the change instead.
--   - The omission of redundant "read on a public repository" rows from the
--     access table (`applyMinVisibility`): a storage optimisation; the index
--     here stores every explicit grant >= read.
--   - Collaborator-plus-team quirk where a collaborator's mode on every unit of
--     an organization repository becomes the access-table maximum (includes
--     team access mode): treated as accidental; see open questions.
--   - go-get meta responses for inaccessible repositories (Go tooling compat).
--   - HTTP status choice (404 vs 403 vs 423): implementation; the rule is that a
--     party who may not see a resource is told it does not exist.
--
-- Emits:
--   - UserLostRepositoryAccess(user, repository)
--       after a recalculation leaves a user with no access to a repository;
--       repositories (watches), issues (assignees, issue watches) react.
--   - SiteAdminImpersonates(admin, target)
--       an API request performed by a site administrator "as" another user (sudo).
--   - RecalculateUserRepositoryAccess(repository, user),
--     RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository),
--     RecalculateUserAccessForRepositories(user, repositories)
--       internal chain; also callable by other modules through
--       AccessIndexMaintenance.
--
-- Reacts to:
--   - repositories/CollaboratorAdded(repository, user, doer)
--   - repositories/CollaboratorAccessChanged(repository, user, doer)
--   - repositories/CollaboratorRemoved(repository, user, doer)
--   - repositories/RepositoryCreated(repository, doer)
--   - repositories/RepositoryTransferred(repository, doer, old_owner_name)
--   - repositories/RepositoryVisibilityChanged(repository, doer)
--   - repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)
--   - organizations/TeamMemberAdded(team, user)
--   - organizations/TeamMemberRemoved(team, user)
--   - organizations/TeamRepositoryAdded(team, repository)
--   - organizations/TeamRepositoryRemoved(team, repository)
--   - organizations/TeamAccessChanged(team)   (access mode, unit access, includes-all)
--   - organizations/TeamDeleted(team)
--   - organizations/OrganizationVisibilityChanged(organization)
--   - accounts/AccountStatusChanged(user)          (restricted flag may have changed)
--   - accounts/UserVisibilityChanged(user, old_visibility, new_visibility)
--   - accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, purge, delete_contributions)

use "./accounts.allium" as accounts
use "./organizations.allium" as organizations
use "./repositories.allium" as repositories
use "./authentication.allium" as authentication
use "./actions.allium" as actions

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Authorization table
------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- Every guarded operation in the forge belongs to exactly one OperationClass.
-- The class fixes (a) which permission the acting party needs, (b) which
-- repository/organization state gates apply, (c) which token scope category a
-- scoped credential must carry (semantics owned by authentication; level is
-- `read` for GET and `write` for POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE).
--
-- Notation: R = target repository, U = unit, P(x,R,U) = effective unit mode
-- (see "Derivation"), "!archived" = refused while R is archived,
-- "!mirror" = refused while R is a pull mirror, "signed" = a signed-in user
-- (an Actions task token counts as signed for API purposes).
--
-- A. Anonymous-capable reads (web + API), refused to anonymous visitors when
--    REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW is set:
--    A1 view repository home / metadata         any unit readable (HasAccess)   scope: repository
--       GET /{o}/{r}, GET /repos/{o}/{r}, /topics (list), /languages, /activities/feeds,
--       /stargazers, /subscribers, /issue_templates, /issue_config
--    A2 read code                                read(code)      scope: repository
--       src/blame/raw/media/archive/commits/compare/branches/tags/git/*/contents GET,
--       editorconfig, statuses GET, signing-key, sync_fork GET, download archives,
--       clone/fetch over HTTP(S) and SSH (git transport, owned by code)
--    A3 read issues                              read(issues)    scope: issue
--       issues list/get/comments/timeline/reactions/labels/milestones/attachments,
--       pinned issues (web also accepts read(pull_requests) for labels/milestones)
--    A4 read pull requests                       read(pull_requests) and read(code), R not empty, R not mirror
--       pulls list/get/diff/patch/commits/files/reviews  scope: repository
--    A5 read releases                            read(releases)  scope: repository
--       releases, release assets, tags-as-releases (draft releases need write(releases))
--    A6 read wiki                                read(wiki)      scope: repository
--    A7 read projects                            read(projects)  (web only)
--    A8 read actions                             read(actions)   scope: repository
--       runs, jobs, logs, artifacts, tasks, workflows list
--    A9 read packages linked to R                read(packages) / package owner visibility (packages)
--    A10 view organization profile, members, teams-list, repos   can_see_organization
--       (private org: members only; limited: signed-in; restricted users: members only)
--    A11 view user profile                       can_see_profile
--       (projects/packages/code pages under an individual: private -> self/site admin only,
--        limited -> signed-in)
--    A12 explore/search users & orgs             signed when REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW or
--       [service.explore] REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW; users page may be disabled entirely
--
-- B. Contributions (signed, read on the unit, R not archived, actor not
--    blocked by R's owner or, for existing conversations, by the poster):
--    B1 open issue                               read(issues)          scope: issue
--    B2 open pull request (from branch or fork)  read(pull_requests), R accepts pulls
--       (not mirror, not empty, unit enabled)   scope: repository
--    B3 comment, react, edit own comment         read(issues|pull_requests); locked
--       conversation additionally needs write(issues|pull_requests)    scope: issue
--    B4 edit own issue title/body/state          poster of an unlocked issue, or write
--    B5 review / request review / resolve conversation   read(pull_requests)
--    B6 fork                                     read(code), forks enabled, may create repo
--       in destination (self, or org where the user may create repositories);
--       a fork of a private repository, or of a repository whose owner is
--       private, is itself private
--    B7 star, watch, subscribe                   any unit readable
--
-- C. Unit writes (signed, write on the unit, !archived):
--    C1 code: push, web editor, create/delete/rename branch, create/delete tag,
--       diff-patch apply, commit notes, sync fork, cherry-pick/revert     write(code), !mirror
--       (branch-scoped: write(code) on R, or maintainer edit delegated by an open
--        PR from that branch; then branch protection rules apply - code)
--    C2 code: commit statuses POST, mirror sync now     write(code) (mirror allowed)
--    C3 issues/pulls triage: labels, milestones, assignees, deadlines, close/reopen others'
--       issues, lock/unlock, dependencies, edit others' issues, time tracking
--       (when restricted to contributors)          write(issues) or write(pull_requests)
--    C4 merge pull request, cancel auto-merge, update PR branch   write(code) on base +
--       merge rules (pulls)
--    C5 releases: create/edit/delete release, release attachments   write(releases)
--    C6 wiki: create/edit/delete page              write(wiki) (or everyone-writable wiki)
--    C7 projects: create/edit columns and cards    write(projects)
--    C8 actions: rerun, cancel, dispatch workflow, delete artifact, approve
--       first-time contributor runs (delegate trust: write(actions) or repo admin)  write(actions)
--
-- D. Repository administration (signed, effective mode >= admin; a restricted
--    credential never confers it):
--    D1 settings (options, units, merge styles, signing, federation), collaborators
--       add/remove/change, teams add/remove, webhooks (unless webhooks disabled),
--       deploy keys, branch/tag protection (create/edit !archived), push mirrors
--       (!archived), topics edit, avatar, issue pin/unpin/move, delete issue,
--       dismiss review, enable/disable workflow, delete action run, LFS locks admin
--    D2 git hooks                                  admin and the user may edit git hooks
--       (site admin or explicitly allowed) and git hooks not disabled instance-wide
--
-- E. Repository ownership actions (effective mode = owner: site admin,
--    owning user, or member of the owning organization's owner team):
--    E1 delete repository, transfer / cancel transfer, convert mirror to normal,
--       convert fork to normal, archive/unarchive, delete wiki, rename wiki branch
--       scope (API delete): user or organization category of R's owner
--    E2 repository-level Actions secrets, variables, runners (API)
--
-- F. Organization operations:
--    F1 org owner (owner-team member or site admin): edit/delete/rename org, members
--       remove, create/edit/delete team, team members & invitations, team repos
--       (plus repo admin on the repo), org labels, org webhooks, org avatar,
--       org Actions secrets/variables/runners, org blocklist, org quota views
--    F2 org member: publicize/conceal own membership, list/search teams
--    F3 team member (or org owner): view team, its members and repositories
--    F4 create repository in org: org owner or member of a team allowed to
--       create repositories
--    F5 org-level unit pages (projects, packages, code search): org unit
--       permission (team unit maximum for members; read for others when the
--       org is visible to them)
--
-- G. Self-service and instance:
--    G1 self or site admin: list/create/delete a user's access tokens
--       (creation/deletion additionally needs password or reverse-proxy auth)
--    G2 signed: own settings, keys, emails, applications, notifications, follow,
--       block/unblock, own repos/orgs, quota
--    G3 site admin (and a credential that allows admin override): /admin/*,
--       repository flags, adopt/delete unadopted repositories, system hooks,
--       instance runners, quota rules/groups, cron, sudo (act as another user)
--    G4 create organization: site admin, or allowed to create orgs and regular
--       org creation not disabled
--
-- Derivation of P(x, R, U) (normative; GetUserRepoPermission):
--   1. Anonymous x: R private -> none. R's owner not public -> none.
--      REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW -> none. Otherwise read on every enabled unit.
--   2. Signed-in x who cannot see R's owner (can_see_owner) and is not a
--      collaborator on R -> none.
--   3. x is site admin, or x is the owning user -> owner on every enabled unit.
--   4. Explicit grant E = strongest of: x's collaboration mode on R; the access
--      mode of every team of R's owning organization that includes R
--      (explicitly or via includes-all) and contains x.
--      If any such team's mode is admin/owner -> that mode on every unit.
--   5. Owning user (not org): every enabled unit gets E, or read when R is
--      public and x is not restricted and E is none; a unit marked
--      everyone-writable gives write to those same non-restricted users.
--   6. Owning organization: each unit gets the strongest of x's collaboration
--      mode and the unit access of each of x's teams that include R; when no
--      team grants that unit and R is public and x is not restricted, the unit
--      falls back to read (write when everyone-writable).
--   7. External wiki / external tracker units never exceed read.
--   8. A restricted credential then reduces every unit mode (reduce_by_credential).
--   9. Operation gates (archived, mirror, blocked, disabled unit) are applied by
--      the operation class, not by P.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- External Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Another component of the forge (a sibling module, a background job) that
-- asks this module to recalculate the explicit-access index or to evaluate the
-- authorization policy. Managed outside this specification.
-- from: models/perm/access/access.go:259
external entity ForgeComponent {
    name: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The authorization policy every other module calls. These are the functions
-- other modules may use in their `requires` clauses (VOCABULARY.md fixes
-- can_read, can_write, is_repo_admin). Each is the closed form of the rules in
-- this file; where they disagree, the rules win.
-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:192
contract AuthorizationPolicy {
    -- P(user, repository, unit) of the derivation above, before operation
    -- gates; user = null means an anonymous visitor.
    unit_access_mode: (user: accounts/User?, repository: repositories/Repository, unit: repositories/UnitKind) -> AccessMode
    -- unit_access_mode >= read and the unit is enabled.
    can_read: (user: accounts/User?, repository: repositories/Repository, unit: repositories/UnitKind) -> Boolean
    -- unit_access_mode >= write, the unit is enabled. Does NOT include the
    -- archived / mirror gates; callers apply the operation class gates.
    can_write: (user: accounts/User?, repository: repositories/Repository, unit: repositories/UnitKind) -> Boolean
    -- can_read on at least one unit (the repository "exists" for the user).
    has_any_access: (user: accounts/User?, repository: repositories/Repository) -> Boolean
    -- repository-wide mode >= admin.
    is_repo_admin: (user: accounts/User?, repository: repositories/Repository) -> Boolean
    -- repository-wide mode = owner.
    is_repo_owner: (user: accounts/User?, repository: repositories/Repository) -> Boolean
    -- may the viewer see the user or organization `owner` (and therefore
    -- anything it owns that is otherwise public)? HasOrgOrUserVisible.
    can_see_owner_user: (viewer: accounts/User?, owner: accounts/User) -> Boolean
    can_see_organization: (viewer: accounts/User?, organization: organizations/Organization) -> Boolean
    -- may the viewer see a user's profile? IsUserVisibleToViewer.
    can_see_profile: (viewer: accounts/User?, target: accounts/User) -> Boolean
    -- may the user be assigned to issues/PRs of the repository: write on any
    -- unit or read on pull requests.
    can_be_assigned: (user: accounts/User, repository: repositories/Repository) -> Boolean
    -- organization-level unit permission (projects, packages, code pages).
    organization_unit_mode: (viewer: accounts/User?, organization: organizations/Organization, unit: repositories/UnitKind) -> AccessMode

    @invariant Monotone
        -- Adding a grant (collaboration, team membership, team repository,
        -- team unit access, site admin flag) never lowers any result;
        -- removing one never raises any result.

    @invariant OwnerDominates
        -- is_repo_owner implies is_repo_admin implies can_write on every
        -- enabled unit whose kind allows write, implies can_read.

    @invariant InvisibleMeansAbsent
        -- When has_any_access is false the repository is reported to the
        -- party as nonexistent; nothing about it (name, existence, redirect
        -- target) is revealed.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Ordered: none < read < write < admin < owner.
-- from: models/perm/access_mode.go:14
enum AccessMode { none | read | write | admin | owner }

-- The classes of guarded operation (see Authorization table).
enum OperationClass {
    read_unit | contribute | write_unit | administer_repository | own_repository
    | view_organization | organization_member | organization_owner | team_member
    | view_profile | site_admin | actions_task
}

-- Why an AccessDecision was granted.
enum GrantBasis {
    site_admin | repository_owner | explicit_grant | public_default
    | everyone_writable | anonymous_public | organization_member
    | organization_owner | team_member | organization_visible | profile_visible
    | self | own_task | public_fallback
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A party making requests with no identity. Exists so that surfaces have
-- someone to face; it carries only the channel it came through.
-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:209
entity AnonymousVisitor {
    channel: web | api | git_http
}

-- The reach of a restricted credential (Forgejo's AuthorizationReducer):
-- fine-grained access tokens and authorized integrations. Derived from the
-- credential by authentication; absent for a normal session or an
-- unrestricted token.
--   all_repositories     no reduction, administrator overrides allowed
--   public_only          only public repositories of public owners keep
--                        their mode; everything else becomes none
--   listed_repositories  listed repositories keep their mode; other public
--                        repositories of public owners are reduced to read;
--                        everything else none
-- Only all_repositories allows site-admin and repo-admin overrides.
-- from: services/authz/authorization_reducer.go:11
entity CredentialRestriction {
    token: authentication/AccessToken?
    reach: all_repositories | public_only | listed_repositories
    listed: Set<repositories/Repository>

    allows_admin_override: reach = all_repositories
}

-- The materialised explicit-access index (Forgejo's `access` table): the
-- strongest explicit grant a user holds on a repository through a
-- collaboration or through teams of the owning organization. The repository
-- owner (user) is never in it. Kept consistent by the recalculation rules.
-- Used for "repositories I can access" listings, assignee and reviewer
-- candidates, readers/writers lists, and as the repository-wide mode in the
-- grant rules below.
-- from: models/perm/access/access.go:25
entity RepoAccess {
    user: accounts/User
    repository: repositories/Repository
    mode: AccessMode
    recalculated_at: Timestamp

    is_admin_grant: mode in {admin, owner}
    is_owner_grant: mode = owner
}

-- The outcome of evaluating one guarded operation for one party. Only granted
-- operations produce a decision; a refusal produces nothing, and the party is
-- told the target does not exist (or, for a visible target, that the operation
-- is forbidden).
-- from: services/context/permission.go:59
entity AccessDecision {
    subject: accounts/User?
    visitor: AnonymousVisitor?
    task: actions/Task?
    repository: repositories/Repository?
    organization: organizations/Organization?
    team: organizations/Team?
    target_user: accounts/User?
    unit_kind: repositories/UnitKind?
    operation: OperationClass
    basis: GrantBasis
    decided_at: Timestamp
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- [service] REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW: anonymous visitors see nothing at all
    -- (web pages, API reads, git over HTTP, SSH anonymous clone).
    require_signin_view: Boolean = false
    -- [service.explore] REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW: explore/search pages and the user
    -- search API need a signed-in user.
    explore_require_signin_view: Boolean = false
    -- [service.explore] DISABLE_USERS_PAGE: the users explore page and user
    -- search API are unavailable.
    explore_disable_users_page: Boolean = false
    -- [repository] DISABLED_REPO_UNITS: unit kinds disabled instance-wide; a
    -- disabled unit is treated as not enabled on every repository (packages
    -- and actions are added automatically when their subsystem is disabled).
    disabled_repo_units: Set<repositories/UnitKind> = {}
    -- [security] DISABLE_GIT_HOOKS: nobody may edit server-side git hooks.
    disable_git_hooks: Boolean = true
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: repository unit reads (signed-in users)
------------------------------------------------------------
-- Trigger UserReadsUnit(subject, unit, credential?) is raised by every
-- operation of class read_unit (table A2-A9). Each rule below is one grant
-- source; the read is permitted when at least one fires.

-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:240
rule ReadUnitAsSiteAdmin {
    when: UserReadsUnit(subject, unit, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    requires: subject.is_admin
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: read_unit, basis: site_admin, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:240
rule ReadUnitAsRepositoryOwner {
    when: UserReadsUnit(subject, unit, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    requires: repository.owner_user = subject
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: read_unit, basis: repository_owner, decided_at: now)
}

-- Collaborators and team members. On a user-owned repository the
-- repository-wide explicit mode applies to every unit; on an organization
-- repository an admin/owner team grant applies to every unit and otherwise the
-- per-unit team access (explicit_unit_mode) decides.
-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:286
rule ReadUnitByExplicitGrant {
    when: UserReadsUnit(subject, unit, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let grant = RepoAccess{user: subject, repository: repository}
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    requires: exists grant
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: grant.is_admin_grant or repository.owner_org = null or explicit_unit_mode(subject, repository, unit.kind) in {read, write, admin, owner}
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: read_unit, basis: explicit_grant, decided_at: now)
}

-- Any non-restricted signed-in user may read every enabled unit of a public
-- repository whose owner they can see. Limited owners are visible to all
-- signed-in users; private organizations only to their members; private
-- users to nobody else.
-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:277
rule ReadUnitByPublicDefault {
    when: UserReadsUnit(subject, unit, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    let owner_visible = (repository.owner_user != null and repository.owner_user.visibility in {public, limited}) or (repository.owner_org != null and (repository.owner_org.visibility in {public, limited} or exists organizations/OrgMembership{organization: repository.owner_org, user: subject}))
    requires: not repository.is_private
    requires: not subject.is_restricted
    requires: owner_visible
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: read_unit, basis: public_default, decided_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: repository unit reads (anonymous visitors)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Anonymous visitors read every enabled unit of a public repository whose
-- owner is public, unless the instance requires sign-in to view anything.
-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:209
rule ReadUnitAnonymously {
    when: AnonymousReadsUnit(visitor, unit)
    let repository = unit.repository
    requires: not config.require_signin_view
    requires: not repository.is_private
    requires: repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    requires: unit.enabled
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(visitor: visitor, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: read_unit, basis: anonymous_public, decided_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: contributions (open issues/PRs, comment, react, review, fork, star)
------------------------------------------------------------
-- UserContributesToRepository(subject, unit, credential?) is raised by table B.
-- Contribution needs read on the unit, a repository that is not archived, and
-- an actor the repository owner has not blocked. Pull requests additionally
-- need a repository that can accept them (not a mirror, not empty, pull
-- requests enabled) - that gate is owned by pulls (table B2).

-- from: services/issue/issue.go:33
rule ContributeAsSiteAdmin {
    when: UserContributesToRepository(subject, unit, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    requires: subject.is_admin
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: repository.owner_user = null or not (exists accounts/UserBlock{blocker: repository.owner_user, blocked: subject})
    requires: repository.owner_org = null or not (exists accounts/UserBlock{blocker_organization: repository.owner_org, blocked: subject})
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (credential?.reach = public_only and not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: contribute, basis: site_admin, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: services/issue/issue.go:33
rule ContributeAsRepositoryOwner {
    when: UserContributesToRepository(subject, unit, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    requires: repository.owner_user = subject
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (credential?.reach = public_only and not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: contribute, basis: repository_owner, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: services/issue/comments.go:51
rule ContributeByExplicitGrant {
    when: UserContributesToRepository(subject, unit, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let grant = RepoAccess{user: subject, repository: repository}
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    requires: exists grant
    requires: grant.is_admin_grant or repository.owner_org = null or explicit_unit_mode(subject, repository, unit.kind) in {read, write, admin, owner}
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: repository.owner_user = null or not (exists accounts/UserBlock{blocker: repository.owner_user, blocked: subject})
    requires: repository.owner_org = null or not (exists accounts/UserBlock{blocker_organization: repository.owner_org, blocked: subject})
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (credential?.reach = public_only and not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: contribute, basis: explicit_grant, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: services/pull/pull.go:42
rule ContributeByPublicDefault {
    when: UserContributesToRepository(subject, unit, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    let owner_visible = (repository.owner_user != null and repository.owner_user.visibility in {public, limited}) or (repository.owner_org != null and (repository.owner_org.visibility in {public, limited} or exists organizations/OrgMembership{organization: repository.owner_org, user: subject}))
    requires: not repository.is_private
    requires: not subject.is_restricted
    requires: owner_visible
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: repository.owner_user = null or not (exists accounts/UserBlock{blocker: repository.owner_user, blocked: subject})
    requires: repository.owner_org = null or not (exists accounts/UserBlock{blocker_organization: repository.owner_org, blocked: subject})
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (credential?.reach = public_only and not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: contribute, basis: public_default, decided_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: unit writes
------------------------------------------------------------
-- UserWritesUnit(subject, unit, changes_git_content, credential?) is raised by
-- table C. Writes are refused on archived repositories, on units that never
-- exceed read (external wiki, external tracker), and - when the operation
-- changes git content - on pull mirrors.

-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:240
rule WriteUnitAsSiteAdmin {
    when: UserWritesUnit(subject, unit, changes_git_content, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    requires: subject.is_admin
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: not unit.is_external
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: not (changes_git_content and repository.is_mirror)
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (credential?.reach = public_only and not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: write_unit, basis: site_admin, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:240
rule WriteUnitAsRepositoryOwner {
    when: UserWritesUnit(subject, unit, changes_git_content, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    requires: repository.owner_user = subject
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: not unit.is_external
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: not (changes_git_content and repository.is_mirror)
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (credential?.reach = public_only and not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: write_unit, basis: repository_owner, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:301
rule WriteUnitByExplicitGrant {
    when: UserWritesUnit(subject, unit, changes_git_content, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let grant = RepoAccess{user: subject, repository: repository}
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    requires: exists grant
    requires: grant.is_admin_grant or (repository.owner_org = null and grant.mode = write) or (repository.owner_org != null and explicit_unit_mode(subject, repository, unit.kind) in {write, admin, owner})
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: not unit.is_external
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: not (changes_git_content and repository.is_mirror)
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (credential?.reach = public_only and not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: write_unit, basis: explicit_grant, decided_at: now)
}

-- A unit marked everyone-writable (Forgejo: the "globally writable" wiki) can
-- be written by any non-restricted signed-in user who can read the public
-- repository.
-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:263
rule WriteUnitByEveryoneWritable {
    when: UserWritesUnit(subject, unit, changes_git_content, credential?)
    let repository = unit.repository
    let owner_public = repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    let owner_visible = (repository.owner_user != null and repository.owner_user.visibility in {public, limited}) or (repository.owner_org != null and (repository.owner_org.visibility in {public, limited} or exists organizations/OrgMembership{organization: repository.owner_org, user: subject}))
    requires: unit.everyone_can_write
    requires: not repository.is_private
    requires: not subject.is_restricted
    requires: owner_visible
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: not (changes_git_content and repository.is_mirror)
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach = all_repositories or (credential?.reach = listed_repositories and repository in credential?.listed) or (credential?.reach = public_only and not repository.is_private and owner_public)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: write_unit, basis: everyone_writable, decided_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: repository administration and ownership
------------------------------------------------------------
-- A restricted credential (anything but all_repositories reach) never
-- confers administration or ownership, even to a site administrator or a
-- repository administrator (AllowAdminOverride = false).

-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_admin.go:14
rule AdministerRepositoryAsSiteAdmin {
    when: UserAdministersRepository(subject, repository, credential?)
    requires: subject.is_admin
    requires: credential = null or credential?.allows_admin_override
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, operation: administer_repository, basis: site_admin, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: services/context/permission.go:19
rule AdministerRepositoryAsOwner {
    when: UserAdministersRepository(subject, repository, credential?)
    requires: repository.owner_user = subject
    requires: credential = null or credential?.allows_admin_override
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, operation: administer_repository, basis: repository_owner, decided_at: now)
}

-- Admin collaborators, admin teams and the owner team.
-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:358
rule AdministerRepositoryByExplicitGrant {
    when: UserAdministersRepository(subject, repository, credential?)
    let grant = RepoAccess{user: subject, repository: repository}
    requires: exists grant
    requires: grant.is_admin_grant
    requires: credential = null or credential?.allows_admin_override
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, operation: administer_repository, basis: explicit_grant, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_owner.go:14
rule OwnRepositoryAsSiteAdmin {
    when: UserPerformsOwnerAction(subject, repository, credential?)
    requires: subject.is_admin
    requires: credential = null or credential?.allows_admin_override
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, operation: own_repository, basis: site_admin, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: routers/web/repo/setting/setting.go:982
rule OwnRepositoryAsOwner {
    when: UserPerformsOwnerAction(subject, repository, credential?)
    requires: repository.owner_user = subject
    requires: credential = null or credential?.allows_admin_override
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, operation: own_repository, basis: repository_owner, decided_at: now)
}

-- Members of the owning organization's owner team hold owner mode.
-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:311
rule OwnRepositoryAsOwnerTeamMember {
    when: UserPerformsOwnerAction(subject, repository, credential?)
    let grant = RepoAccess{user: subject, repository: repository}
    requires: exists grant
    requires: grant.is_owner_grant
    requires: credential = null or credential?.allows_admin_override
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, repository: repository, operation: own_repository, basis: explicit_grant, decided_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: Actions task tokens
------------------------------------------------------------
-- A running Actions task authenticates with its own token. On the repository
-- that runs it, it has write (read only when the run was triggered by a pull
-- request from a fork). On any other repository it is an unprivileged
-- identity that can only read public repositories of public owners.

-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:143
rule TaskAccessesOwnRepository {
    when: ActionsTaskAccessesRepository(task, unit, level)
    let repository = unit.repository
    requires: task.job.run.repository = repository
    requires: unit.enabled
    requires: level = read or (level = write and not task.is_fork_pull_request and not repository.is_archived)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(task: task, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: actions_task, basis: own_task, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/repo_access.go:14
rule TaskReadsOtherPublicRepository {
    when: ActionsTaskAccessesRepository(task, unit, level)
    let repository = unit.repository
    requires: task.job.run.repository != repository
    requires: level = read
    requires: not repository.is_private
    requires: repository.owner_user?.visibility = public or repository.owner_org?.visibility = public
    requires: unit.enabled
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(task: task, repository: repository, unit_kind: unit.kind, operation: actions_task, basis: public_fallback, decided_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: organizations and teams
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: models/organization/org.go:475
rule ViewOrganizationAsSiteAdmin {
    when: UserViewsOrganization(subject, organization)
    requires: subject.is_admin
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, organization: organization, operation: view_organization, basis: site_admin, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: services/context/org.go:128
rule ViewOrganizationAsMember {
    when: UserViewsOrganization(subject, organization)
    requires: exists organizations/OrgMembership{organization: organization, user: subject}
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, organization: organization, operation: view_organization, basis: organization_member, decided_at: now)
}

-- Public and limited organizations are visible to every non-restricted
-- signed-in user; restricted users see only organizations they belong to.
-- from: services/context/org.go:122
rule ViewOrganizationByVisibility {
    when: UserViewsOrganization(subject, organization)
    requires: organization.visibility in {public, limited}
    requires: not subject.is_restricted
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, organization: organization, operation: view_organization, basis: organization_visible, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: services/context/org.go:122
rule ViewOrganizationAnonymously {
    when: AnonymousViewsOrganization(visitor, organization)
    requires: organization.visibility = public
    requires: not config.require_signin_view
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(visitor: visitor, organization: organization, operation: view_organization, basis: organization_visible, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_org_membership.go:12
rule ActAsOrganizationMemberAsSiteAdmin {
    when: UserActsAsOrganizationMember(subject, organization, credential?)
    requires: subject.is_admin
    requires: credential = null or credential?.allows_admin_override
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, organization: organization, operation: organization_member, basis: site_admin, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_org_membership.go:12
rule ActAsOrganizationMember {
    when: UserActsAsOrganizationMember(subject, organization, credential?)
    requires: exists organizations/OrgMembership{organization: organization, user: subject}
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach != public_only or organization.visibility = public
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, organization: organization, operation: organization_member, basis: organization_member, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_org_ownership.go:12
rule ActAsOrganizationOwnerAsSiteAdmin {
    when: UserActsAsOrganizationOwner(subject, organization, credential?)
    requires: subject.is_admin
    requires: credential = null or credential?.allows_admin_override
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, organization: organization, operation: organization_owner, basis: site_admin, decided_at: now)
}

-- Organization owners are exactly the members of its owner team.
-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_org_ownership.go:12
rule ActAsOrganizationOwner {
    when: UserActsAsOrganizationOwner(subject, organization, credential?)
    requires: exists organizations/TeamMembership{team: organization.owners_team, user: subject}
    requires: credential = null or credential?.reach != public_only or organization.visibility = public
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, organization: organization, operation: organization_owner, basis: organization_owner, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_team_membership.go:12
rule ActAsTeamMemberAsSiteAdmin {
    when: UserActsAsTeamMember(subject, team, credential?)
    requires: subject.is_admin
    requires: credential = null or credential?.allows_admin_override
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, team: team, organization: team.organization, operation: team_member, basis: site_admin, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_team_membership.go:20
rule ActAsTeamMemberAsOrganizationOwner {
    when: UserActsAsTeamMember(subject, team, credential?)
    requires: exists organizations/TeamMembership{team: team.organization.owners_team, user: subject}
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, team: team, organization: team.organization, operation: team_member, basis: organization_owner, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_team_membership.go:28
rule ActAsTeamMember {
    when: UserActsAsTeamMember(subject, team, credential?)
    requires: exists organizations/TeamMembership{team: team, user: subject}
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, team: team, organization: team.organization, operation: team_member, basis: team_member, decided_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: user profiles
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: models/user/user.go:1405
rule ViewOwnProfileOrAsSiteAdmin {
    when: UserViewsProfile(subject, target)
    requires: subject = target or subject.is_admin
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, target_user: target, operation: view_profile, basis: self, decided_at: now)
}

-- Public profiles are visible to all; limited profiles to non-restricted
-- signed-in users.
-- from: models/user/user.go:1410
rule ViewProfileByVisibility {
    when: UserViewsProfile(subject, target)
    requires: target.visibility = public or (target.visibility = limited and not subject.is_restricted)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, target_user: target, operation: view_profile, basis: profile_visible, decided_at: now)
}

-- A private profile is visible to a non-restricted viewer whom the target
-- follows, or who shares an organization with the target.
-- from: models/user/user.go:1418
rule ViewPrivateProfileByRelationship {
    when: UserViewsProfile(subject, target)
    requires: target.visibility = private
    requires: not subject.is_restricted
    requires: exists accounts/Follow{follower: target, followee: subject} or shares_organization(target, subject)
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, target_user: target, operation: view_profile, basis: profile_visible, decided_at: now)
}

-- from: models/user/user.go:1410
rule ViewProfileAnonymously {
    when: AnonymousViewsProfile(visitor, target)
    requires: target.visibility = public
    requires: not config.require_signin_view
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(visitor: visitor, target_user: target, operation: view_profile, basis: profile_visible, decided_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: site administration and impersonation
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_site_admin.go:12
rule ActAsSiteAdmin {
    when: UserActsAsSiteAdmin(subject, credential?)
    requires: subject.is_admin
    requires: credential = null or credential?.allows_admin_override
    ensures: AccessDecision.created(subject: subject, operation: site_admin, basis: site_admin, decided_at: now)
}

-- A site administrator may perform an API request as another (existing)
-- user; every permission check of that request is then made for the target.
-- from: routers/api/v1/api.go:96
rule SiteAdminSudo {
    when: SiteAdminActsAs(admin, target)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: target != admin
    ensures: SiteAdminImpersonates(admin: admin, target: target)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: explicit-access index recalculation
------------------------------------------------------------
-- The index row for (user, repository) always equals explicit_mode(user,
-- repository): the strongest of the user's collaboration mode and the access
-- mode of each team of the owning organization that includes the repository
-- and contains the user. It is recalculated whenever an input changes.

-- from: models/perm/access/access.go:277
rule RecalculateOneUsersAccess {
    when: RecalculateUserRepositoryAccess(repository, user)
    let mode = explicit_mode(user, repository)
    let existing = RepoAccess{user: user, repository: repository}
    requires: repository.owner_user != user
    ensures:
        if mode = none:
            not exists existing
        else:
            if exists existing:
                existing.mode = mode
                existing.recalculated_at = now
            else:
                RepoAccess.created(user: user, repository: repository, mode: mode, recalculated_at: now)
}

-- After a recalculation, a user who can no longer reach the repository at all
-- loses everything that presumed access: other modules unwatch the
-- repository, drop issue subscriptions and unassign the user.
-- from: models/org_team.go:556
rule AnnounceLostAccess {
    when: RecalculateUserRepositoryAccess(repository, user)
    requires: not has_any_access(user, repository)
    ensures: UserLostRepositoryAccess(user: user, repository: repository)
}

-- Full recalculation for one repository: every user who holds or held an
-- explicit grant.
-- from: models/perm/access/access.go:285
rule RecalculateWholeRepository {
    when: RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository)
    ensures:
        for user in explicit_grantees(repository):
            RecalculateUserRepositoryAccess(repository: repository, user: user)
    ensures:
        for stale in RepoAccesses where repository = repository:
            RecalculateUserRepositoryAccess(repository: repository, user: stale.user)
}

-- from: models/perm/access/access.go:291
rule RecalculateUserAcrossRepositories {
    when: RecalculateUserAccessForRepositories(user, repositories)
    ensures:
        for repository in repositories:
            RecalculateUserRepositoryAccess(repository: repository, user: user)
}

-- Reactions: when each input of explicit_mode changes.

-- from: modules/repository/collaborator.go:44
rule RecalculateOnCollaboratorAdded {
    when: repositories/CollaboratorAdded(repository, user, _)
    ensures: RecalculateUserRepositoryAccess(repository: repository, user: user)
}

-- from: modules/repository/collaborator.go:80
rule RecalculateOnCollaboratorAccessChanged {
    when: repositories/CollaboratorAccessChanged(repository, user, _)
    ensures: RecalculateUserRepositoryAccess(repository: repository, user: user)
}

-- from: modules/repository/collaborator.go:106
rule RecalculateOnCollaboratorRemoved {
    when: repositories/CollaboratorRemoved(repository, user, _)
    ensures: RecalculateUserRepositoryAccess(repository: repository, user: user)
}

-- New organization repositories are picked up by includes-all teams.
-- from: modules/repository/create.go:151
rule RecalculateOnRepositoryCreated {
    when: repositories/RepositoryCreated(repository, _)
    ensures: RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository: repository)
}

-- from: services/repository/transfer.go:192
rule RecalculateOnRepositoryTransferred {
    when: repositories/RepositoryTransferred(repository, _, _)
    ensures: RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository: repository)
}

-- from: modules/repository/create.go:262
rule RecalculateOnVisibilityChanged {
    when: repositories/RepositoryVisibilityChanged(repository, _)
    ensures: RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository: repository)
}

-- from: services/repository/delete.go:440
rule DropAccessOnRepositoryDeleted {
    when: repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, _)
    ensures:
        for row in RepoAccesses where repository = repository:
            not exists row
}

-- from: models/org_team.go:431
rule RecalculateOnTeamMemberAdded {
    when: organizations/TeamMemberAdded(team, user)
    ensures: RecalculateUserAccessForRepositories(user: user, repositories: team_repositories(team))
}

-- from: models/org_team.go:494
rule RecalculateOnTeamMemberRemoved {
    when: organizations/TeamMemberRemoved(team, user)
    ensures: RecalculateUserAccessForRepositories(user: user, repositories: team_repositories(team))
}

-- from: models/org_team.go:49
rule RecalculateOnTeamRepositoryAdded {
    when: organizations/TeamRepositoryAdded(team, repository)
    ensures: RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository: repository)
}

-- from: models/org_team.go:135
rule RecalculateOnTeamRepositoryRemoved {
    when: organizations/TeamRepositoryRemoved(team, repository)
    ensures: RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository: repository)
}

-- Access mode, per-unit access, or includes-all changed.
-- from: models/org_team.go:297
rule RecalculateOnTeamAccessChanged {
    when: organizations/TeamAccessChanged(team)
    ensures:
        for repository in organization_repositories(team.organization):
            RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository: repository)
}

-- from: models/org_team.go:316
rule RecalculateOnTeamDeleted {
    when: organizations/TeamDeleted(team)
    ensures:
        for repository in organization_repositories(team.organization):
            RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository: repository)
}

-- Not recalculated by Forgejo; required for the index to stay consistent
-- with has_any_access (see open questions). AccountStatusChanged covers the
-- restricted flag.
-- from: services/user/update.go:109
rule RecalculateOnUserRestrictionChanged {
    when: accounts/AccountStatusChanged(user)
    ensures:
        for row in RepoAccesses where user = user:
            RecalculateUserRepositoryAccess(repository: row.repository, user: user)
}

-- Repositories of a user whose visibility changed may have become
-- (in)visible to non-collaborators; announce lost access where it applies.
-- from: models/organization/org.go:475
rule RecalculateOnOwnerVisibilityChanged {
    when: accounts/UserVisibilityChanged(user, _, _)
    ensures:
        for repository in owned_repositories(user):
            RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository: repository)
}

-- from: models/organization/org.go:475
rule RecalculateOnOrganizationVisibilityChanged {
    when: organizations/OrganizationVisibilityChanged(organization)
    ensures:
        for repository in organization_repositories(organization):
            RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository: repository)
}

-- from: services/user/delete.go:106
rule DropAccessOnUserDeleted {
    when: accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, _, _)
    ensures:
        for row in RepoAccesses where user = user:
            not exists row
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- One index row per (user, repository).
invariant OneAccessRowPerUserAndRepository {
    for a in RepoAccesses:
        for b in RepoAccesses:
            (a.user = b.user and a.repository = b.repository) implies a = b
}

-- The index only records real grants, never `none`.
invariant AccessRowsAreGrants {
    for a in RepoAccesses:
        a.mode != none
}

-- The owning user is never in the index; ownership is structural.
invariant OwnerIsNotIndexed {
    for a in RepoAccesses:
        a.repository.owner_user != a.user
}

-- A collaboration confers at most admin; owner comes only from ownership or
-- the owner team.
-- from: modules/repository/collaborator.go:49
invariant CollaborationNeverOwner {
    for c in repositories/Collaborations:
        c.access_mode in {read, write, admin}
}

-- The index row always equals the derivation.
invariant AccessIndexMatchesDerivation {
    for a in RepoAccesses:
        a.mode = explicit_mode(a.user, a.repository)
}

-- Instance-wide disabled units are never enabled on any repository.
-- from: models/repo/repo_unit.go:360
invariant DisabledUnitsAreNeverEnabled {
    for u in repositories/RepoUnits:
        u.kind in config.disabled_repo_units implies not u.enabled
}

-- External units can be read but never written.
-- from: models/unit/unit.go:278
invariant ExternalUnitsAreReadOnly {
    for d in AccessDecisions:
        d.operation = write_unit implies d.unit_kind not in {external_wiki, external_tracker}
}

-- Nothing is ever granted to an anonymous visitor on a private repository, or
-- on any repository when sign-in is required.
invariant AnonymousNeverSeesPrivate {
    for d in AccessDecisions:
        (d.visitor != null and d.repository != null) implies (not d.repository.is_private and not config.require_signin_view)
}

-- Archived repositories are read-only for content.
invariant ArchivedIsReadOnly {
    for d in AccessDecisions:
        (d.operation in {write_unit, contribute} and d.repository != null) implies not d.repository.is_archived
}

-- Restricted users are only ever granted through explicit grants, ownership,
-- organization membership, or the site-admin flag.
invariant RestrictedUsersOnlyThroughExplicitGrants {
    for d in AccessDecisions:
        (d.subject != null and d.subject.is_restricted) implies d.basis not in {public_default, everyone_writable, organization_visible}
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Anyone signed in with a usable account.
actor SignedInUser {
    identified_by: accounts/User where is_active = true and prohibit_login = false
}

-- A signed-in user the administrator has restricted: sees only repositories
-- and organizations explicitly granted to them.
actor RestrictedUser {
    identified_by: accounts/User where is_restricted = true and prohibit_login = false
}

actor SiteAdministrator {
    identified_by: accounts/User where is_admin = true and prohibit_login = false
}

-- A running Actions task presenting its automatic token.
actor RunningTask {
    identified_by: actions/Task where status = running
}

-- A sibling component of the forge using the authorization service.
actor ForgeInternals {
    identified_by: ForgeComponent where name != null
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- What an anonymous visitor can see and read on a repository. The surface
-- exists only for enabled units of public repositories of public owners;
-- for anything else there is nothing to face (the repository "does not
-- exist"). REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW removes it entirely (rule ReadUnitAnonymously).
-- Web: GET /{owner}/{repo}/... read routes grouped under `ignSignIn`.
-- API: GET /api/v1/repos/{owner}/{repo}/... read routes (repoAssignment +
-- repoAccess, no reqToken). Git: anonymous HTTP clone/fetch of public repos.
surface AnonymousRepositoryAccess {
    facing visitor: AnonymousVisitor

    context unit: repositories/RepoUnit where enabled and not repository.is_private and ((repository.owner_user != null and repository.owner_user.visibility = public) or (repository.owner_org != null and repository.owner_org.visibility = public))

    exposes:
        visitor.channel
        unit.kind
        unit.repository.name

    provides:
        AnonymousReadsUnit(visitor, unit)

    @guarantee PrivateRepositoriesDoNotExist
        -- A private repository, a repository of a non-public owner, or any
        -- repository when sign-in is required is answered exactly as a
        -- repository that does not exist.

    @guidance
        -- Anonymous SSH access is never possible (SSH needs a key);
        -- SSH_EXPOSE_ANONYMOUS only affects whether the clone URL is shown.
}

-- Which repositories a signed-in user can see at all (has_any_access):
-- listings, search, the repository header, redirects. Owned, explicitly
-- granted, administered (site admin), or public with a visible owner for a
-- non-restricted user.
-- Web: dashboard, explore, /{owner}; API: /repos/search, /user/repos,
-- /users/{u}/repos, /orgs/{org}/repos (AccessibleRepositoryCondition).
surface VisibleRepository {
    facing user: SignedInUser

    context repository: repositories/Repository where owner_user = user or user.is_admin or exists RepoAccess{user: user, repository: this} or (not is_private and not user.is_restricted and ((owner_user != null and owner_user.visibility in {public, limited}) or (owner_org != null and (owner_org.visibility in {public, limited} or exists organizations/OrgMembership{organization: owner_org, user: user}))))

    exposes:
        repository.name
        repository.is_private
        repository.is_archived
        repository.is_mirror
        has_any_access(user, repository)

    @guarantee SameAnswerEverywhere
        -- Listings, search results, direct links, API lookups by id and
        -- redirects after a rename all apply the same visibility; a
        -- repository hidden here is hidden everywhere.
}

-- What a signed-in user can do on one unit of a repository (tables A-C).
-- Web: routes under `{username}/{reponame}` with reqRepoCodeReader,
-- reqRepoIssueReader, reqRepoPullsReader, reqRepoReleaseReader,
-- reqRepoProjectsReader, reqRepoActionsReader, reqRepoCodeWriter,
-- reqRepoReleaseWriter, reqRepoWikiWriter, reqRepoIssuesOrPullsWriter,
-- reqRepoProjectsWriter, reqRepoActionsWriter, canEnableEditor,
-- RepoMustNotBeArchived. API: reqRepoReader(unit), reqRepoWriter(units...),
-- reqRepoBranchWriter, mustNotBeArchived, mustEnableIssues,
-- mustEnableIssuesOrPulls, mustAllowPulls, mustEnableWiki,
-- reqIssueUnlockedOrCanWrite, reqEditIssue.
surface RepositoryUnitAccess {
    facing user: SignedInUser

    context unit: repositories/RepoUnit

    exposes:
        unit.kind
        unit.enabled
        unit.repository.is_archived
        unit.repository.is_mirror
        can_read(user, unit.repository, unit.kind)
        can_write(user, unit.repository, unit.kind)

    provides:
        UserReadsUnit(user, unit, credential)
        UserContributesToRepository(user, unit, credential)
            when not unit.repository.is_archived
        UserWritesUnit(user, unit, changes_git_content, credential)
            when not unit.repository.is_archived

    @guarantee UnitMustBeEnabled
        -- An operation on a disabled unit (per repository or instance-wide)
        -- is answered as not found, whatever the user's mode.

    @guarantee ArchivedRefusesWrites
        -- On an archived repository every content write and contribution is
        -- refused (the API answers "locked"); reads are unaffected.

    @guarantee MirrorCodeIsReadOnly
        -- On a pull mirror, pushes, web edits, branch/tag creation and pull
        -- requests into it are refused; "sync now" (write on code) is allowed.

    @guidance
        -- Web and API share this boundary. The web additionally hides write
        -- controls the user may not use (CanWriteCode, CanWriteIssues,
        -- CanWritePulls, CanWriteActions) and hides draft releases from
        -- users without write on releases.
}

-- Repository administration and ownership (tables D, E).
-- Web: /{owner}/{repo}/settings/* (reqSignIn + reqRepoAdmin; delete,
-- transfer, convert, archive, wiki delete require IsOwner).
-- API: reqAdmin(), reqOwner(), PATCH/DELETE /repos/{o}/{r},
-- /collaborators, /teams, /hooks, /keys, /branch_protections,
-- /tag_protections, /push_mirrors, /topics PUT, /avatar, /transfer,
-- /convert, /actions/{secrets,variables,runners}, /hooks/git.
surface RepositoryAdministration {
    facing user: SignedInUser

    context repository: repositories/Repository

    exposes:
        is_repo_admin(user, repository)
        is_repo_owner(user, repository)

    provides:
        UserAdministersRepository(user, repository, credential)
        UserPerformsOwnerAction(user, repository, credential)

    @guarantee FineGrainedTokensCannotAdminister
        -- A credential restricted to public repositories or to listed
        -- repositories never confers repository administration or ownership.

    @guidance
        -- Git hooks editing additionally requires that the user may edit git
        -- hooks (site admin or per-user allowance) and that git hooks are not
        -- disabled instance-wide (config.disable_git_hooks).
}

-- Who holds explicit access, as seen by the repository's administrators
-- (settings > collaborators / teams; API collaborators list and
-- permission report).
surface ExplicitAccessList {
    facing user: SignedInUser

    context repository: repositories/Repository where owner_user = user or user.is_admin or exists RepoAccess{user: user, repository: this, mode: admin} or exists RepoAccess{user: user, repository: this, mode: owner}

    exposes:
        for grant in RepoAccesses where repository = repository:
            grant.user
            grant.mode
}

-- What a signed-in user can learn about the restriction carried by the
-- credential they are using (fine-grained token, authorized integration).
-- Web: token creation and listing pages; API: GET /users/{username}/tokens.
surface CredentialReach {
    facing user: SignedInUser

    context credential: CredentialRestriction

    exposes:
        credential.reach
        credential.allows_admin_override
        for repository in credential.listed:
            repository.name

    @guarantee ReductionNeverRaises
        -- A credential restriction only ever lowers the mode the user would
        -- otherwise hold; it never grants anything.
}

-- Permission reporting endpoints.
-- API: GET /repos/{o}/{r}/collaborators/{collaborator}/permission (any
-- repository reader may ask about any collaborator), GET
-- /users/{username}/orgs/{org}/permissions.
surface PermissionReport {
    facing user: SignedInUser

    context repository: repositories/Repository

    exposes:
        has_any_access(user, repository)
        unit_access_mode(user, repository, code)
        is_repo_admin(user, repository)

    @guidance
        -- The organization permission report returns, for a user and an
        -- organization: is_owner, is_admin (admin team), can_write,
        -- can_read, can_create_repository.
}

-- Org-level authority (table F). Web: /org/{org}/* with
-- OrgAssignment(requireMember, requireOwner, requireTeamMember,
-- requireTeamAdmin). API: /orgs/{org}/* with reqOrgOwnership,
-- reqOrgMembership; /teams/{id}/* with reqTeamMembership.
surface OrganizationAccess {
    facing user: SignedInUser

    context organization: organizations/Organization

    provides:
        UserViewsOrganization(user, organization)
        UserActsAsOrganizationMember(user, organization, credential)
        UserActsAsOrganizationOwner(user, organization, credential)

    @guarantee HiddenOrganizationsDoNotExist
        -- A private organization is answered as nonexistent to non-members;
        -- a limited or private one to anonymous visitors; any organization a
        -- restricted user is not a member of, to that user.
}

-- The organizations a signed-in user can see (can_see_organization).
surface VisibleOrganization {
    facing user: SignedInUser

    context organization: organizations/Organization where user.is_admin or exists organizations/OrgMembership{organization: this, user: user} or (visibility in {public, limited} and not user.is_restricted)

    exposes:
        organization.name
        organization.visibility
}

-- The organizations an anonymous visitor can see.
surface AnonymousOrganizationAccess {
    facing visitor: AnonymousVisitor

    context organization: organizations/Organization where visibility = public

    exposes:
        organization.name

    provides:
        AnonymousViewsOrganization(visitor, organization)
}

surface TeamAccess {
    facing user: SignedInUser

    context team: organizations/Team

    provides:
        UserActsAsTeamMember(user, team, credential)

    @guidance
        -- Non-members of the organization are told the team does not exist;
        -- members of the organization outside the team are told it is
        -- forbidden. Owners and members of an includes-all admin team see
        -- every team.
}

-- Profile visibility. Web: /{username}, /{username}/-/projects,
-- /{username}/-/packages (individualPermsChecker). API: GET
-- /users/{username}, /users/search (reqExploreSignIn,
-- reqUsersExploreEnabled).
surface ProfileAccess {
    facing user: SignedInUser

    context target: accounts/User

    provides:
        UserViewsProfile(user, target)
}

-- The profiles a signed-in user can see (can_see_profile).
surface VisibleProfile {
    facing user: SignedInUser

    context target: accounts/User where this = user or user.is_admin or visibility = public or (visibility = limited and not user.is_restricted) or (visibility = private and not user.is_restricted and (exists accounts/Follow{follower: this, followee: user} or shares_organization(this, user)))

    exposes:
        target.name
        target.visibility
}

-- The profiles an anonymous visitor can see.
surface AnonymousProfileAccess {
    facing visitor: AnonymousVisitor

    context target: accounts/User where visibility = public

    exposes:
        target.name

    provides:
        AnonymousViewsProfile(visitor, target)
}

-- Instance administration gate (table G3). Web: /-/admin/* (reqSignIn +
-- site admin). API: /admin/* (tokenRequiresScopes(admin), reqToken,
-- reqSiteAdmin); any API request may carry `sudo`.
surface SiteAdministration {
    facing admin: SiteAdministrator

    provides:
        UserActsAsSiteAdmin(admin, credential)
        SiteAdminActsAs(admin, target)

    @guarantee OnlyAdministratorsImpersonate
        -- A sudo request from anyone but a site administrator is refused
        -- outright and is never silently ignored.
}

-- What a running Actions task can do with its automatic token.
-- API: every /repos/{o}/{r}/* route accepts the task token
-- (RepoAccess check), reqToken treats it as signed.
surface ActionsTaskAccess {
    facing task: RunningTask

    context unit: repositories/RepoUnit

    provides:
        ActionsTaskAccessesRepository(task, unit, level)

    @guarantee ForkRunsAreReadOnly
        -- A run triggered by a pull request from a fork never writes to the
        -- repository it runs in.
}

-- The authorization service and access-index maintenance offered to every
-- other module.
surface AccessIndexMaintenance {
    facing component: ForgeInternals

    context repository: repositories/Repository

    exposes:
        component.name
        for grant in RepoAccesses where repository = repository:
            grant.user
            grant.mode

    provides:
        RecalculateUserRepositoryAccess(repository, user)
        RecalculateRepositoryAccess(repository)
        RecalculateUserAccessForRepositories(user, repositories)

    contracts:
        fulfils AuthorizationPolicy

    @guarantee RecalculationIsAtomic
        -- A recalculation and the change that caused it commit together; no
        -- request ever observes the new grant inputs with the old index.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred AuthorizationPolicy.explicit_unit_mode    -- see: access.allium "Derivation" step 6: strongest of collaboration mode and the unit access of each team that includes the repository (organizations/TeamUnitAccess)

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Forgejo does not recalculate the access index when a user's restricted flag or an owner's visibility changes; the index is only an optimisation there. Should a rebuild recalculate (as specified here) or never depend on the index for those decisions?"
open question "On an organization repository a user who is both a collaborator and a team member gets the access-table maximum (including the team's access mode) on every unit, bypassing per-unit team limits. Accidental (spec assumes per-unit strongest of collaboration and team unit access) or intended?"
open question "Anonymous visitors cannot read individual public units of a private repository (TODO in GetUserRepoPermission). Should per-unit anonymous/public access on private repositories be supported?"
open question "Everyone-writable is only offered for the wiki unit. Should the per-unit default permission for signed-in users (and an anonymous access mode) be generalised to every unit?"
open question "A site administrator using a fine-grained token keeps owner mode on repositories the token reaches but loses the admin override on admin-only endpoints. Is that asymmetry intended?"
open question "Actions task tokens are treated as signed-in for reqToken but have no user; should organization-level endpoints accept them?"
open question "Visibility of repositories after a repository is made private: forks inherit privacy and stars are cleared (repositories). Should watches and issue subscriptions of users who lost access be cleared immediately via UserLostRepositoryAccess as specified?"

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Requests to other modules
------------------------------------------------------------
-- REQUEST repositories/Collaborations, repositories/RepoUnits: entity collection names used by invariants CollaborationNeverOwner and DisabledUnitsAreNeverEnabled.
-- REQUEST repositories: react to access/UserLostRepositoryAccess(user, repository) by removing the user's watch (WatchRepoExplicitly none).
-- REQUEST issues: react to access/UserLostRepositoryAccess(user, repository) by removing the user's issue subscriptions and the assignments that access/can_be_assigned no longer allows.
-- REQUEST repositories: its local predicates can_see_repository / can_read_code / can_write_code / is_repo_admin / is_repo_owner map to access/has_any_access, can_read(.., code), can_write(.., code), is_repo_admin, is_repo_owner.
-- REQUEST accounts/AccountStatusChanged(user): must be emitted when is_restricted changes (drives RecalculateOnUserRestrictionChanged).
-- REQUEST accounts/User.allow_git_hook is used for table D2 (git hooks editing).
-- REQUEST authentication: derive access/CredentialRestriction from authentication/AccessToken (all_repositories and not public_only -> all_repositories; public_only -> public_only; not all_repositories -> listed_repositories with `repositories`) and likewise from AuthorizedIntegration; scope-category checks stay in authentication (table column "scope").
-- REQUEST actions: Task reaches its repository as task.job.run.repository; access treats status = running as the token being usable.
-- REQUEST pulls/PullRequest.allow_maintainer_edit: Boolean; branch-scoped write delegation (table C1).
-- REQUEST organizations: owned black boxes organization_repositories(organization) and team_repositories(team) (includes-all teams cover every organization repository).
-- REQUEST accounts: owned black box owned_repositories(user) (repositories owned by a user) - or repositories provides it.
